      "id": "sol.ahsme-1981-p3.live",
      "kind": "proof-sketch",
      "text": "Using the common denominator \\(6x\\) gives \\[ \\begin{aligned} \\frac1x+\\frac1{2x}+\\frac1{3x} &=\\frac6{6x}+\\frac3{6x}\\\\ &\\quad+\\frac2{6x}\\\\ &=\\frac{11}{6x}. \\end{aligned} \\]\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is D.",
